{{!--
  Handlebars template used by `scripts/bench_weights.sh` for pallets whose
  `weights.rs` owns the `WeightInfo` trait itself.

  The shared `templates/weights-template.hbs` emits only `SubstrateWeight<T>`
  because most pallets declare `WeightInfo` in `lib.rs`. `pallet-belize-oracle`
  declares it in `weights.rs` (as `pallet-belize-moderation` does), so using the
  shared template would delete the trait and break the build.

  Both templates emit `impl ... super::WeightInfo for SubstrateWeight<T>` when the
  pallet has its own trait, so the built-in FRAME template — which emits a
  `WeightInfo<T>` struct and no `SubstrateWeight` at all — is wrong for this
  repository either way.

  `T::DbWeight` is used rather than a hard-coded `RocksDbWeight` so the weights
  follow the runtime's configured database weight. On the current runtime
  `DbWeight = RocksDbWeight`, so the numbers are identical; the indirection just
  keeps them correct if that ever changes.
--}}
